Source/type mix, rejects and confidence distribution
Freshness lag, missing events and reconciliation gap
Source: ledger + telemetry + audit version registry
Daily trends / weekly quality / monthly governance
Stale or missing data = Unknown, never green / zero
Critical error → hold; changes require requalification" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontColor=#17324d;fontStyle=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="report-12"><mxGeometry x="20" y="70" width="705" height="175" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="reporting-footer" value="GLOBAL FILTERS: UTC cohort / environment / fax type (including unknown) / approved source ID / auto vs human / model-schema-mapping / destination.
EXECUTIVE: volume, yield, accuracy, SLA, cost. OPERATIONS: backlog, stage latency, HL7 failures, retries. QUALITY: audits, error bounds and drift.
Proposed read-only reporting path: job/manifest facts + safe telemetry + independent audits + billing → governed aggregates → role-scoped dashboard.
Use unsampled reconciled records for business totals. Retries, multiple routes and corrected revisions must not inflate unique-fax success counts.
All targets remain proposed. Page 3 defines release qualification; this page defines monitoring. See ../docs/reporting-metrics.md for metric formulas.
New HL7 / review / type and reporting stages require implementation. No live metrics, clinical data or monitoring resources were accessed." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=19;fontColor=#63758a;fontStyle=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="65" y="1820" width="2250" height="150" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
